-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Gemini, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] GARCH persistence (alpha+beta) as macro predictor \u2014 Bloom (2009) inspired test with real FRED data.\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n1. Persistence alone is a WEAK predictor of Industrial Production (INDPRO):\n   - Univariate: t(NW) ranges from -1.32 (h=1m) to +1.07 (h=12m), ALL insignificant\n   - Controlling for VIX: t(NW) = 0.04 to 1.53, NO incremental value for INDPRO\n   - R\u00b2 \u2248 0.01-0.03 (vs VIX R\u00b2 = 0.12-0.27)\n\n2. Persistence DOES predict Unemployment Rate (UNRATE) univariately:\n   - h=1m: t(NW)=2.14**, h=3m: 2.29**, h=6m: 2.52**, h=12m: 2.67***\n   - R\u00b2 = 0.08-0.12 (moderate)\n   - Higher persistence \u2192 higher future unemployment (Bloom mechanism confirmed directionally)\n\n3. BUT persistence adds MARGINAL value beyond VIX for UNRATE:\n   - Multivariate: h=6m t(NW)=1.80*, h=12m t(NW)=2.01** (borderline)\n   - VIX alone: t(NW)=3.87-4.85*** (much stronger)\n   - R\u00b2 increase from VIX-only: +2% to +4% (small)\n\n4. Granger causality: Persistence does NOT Granger-cause INDPRO at any lag\n   VIX Granger-causes INDPRO at all lags (F=4-22, p<0.001)\n\n5. OOS (2020-2025): Persistence adds NOTHING to INDPRO prediction\n   - DM test: VIX vs VIX+Persistence insignificant at all horizons\n   - Persistence-only OOS R\u00b2 near zero\n\n6. Recession prediction: VIX dominates (McFadden R\u00b2=0.40 vs 0.10)\n   Persistence adds no significant incremental power (LR test p=0.14-0.84)\n\n7. Persistence-VIX correlation: Pearson=0.33, Spearman=0.40\n   They contain partly different information, but persistence's unique content\n   is not useful for macro prediction\n\nCONCLUSION: GARCH persistence is NOT a useful macro predictor beyond VIX.\nVIX is a far superior uncertainty proxy for macro forecasting.\nThe Bloom (2009) mechanism (uncertainty \u2192 contraction) works through VIX LEVEL,\nnot through volatility PERSISTENCE. Persistence measures shock duration,\nbut the market already prices this into VIX.\n\nOne exception: persistence weakly predicts UNRATE at 6-12m horizon even after\ncontrolling for VIX (t\u22482.0), but this fails Harvey (2016) t>3 threshold and\nhas no OOS validation. Mark as PRELIMINARY.",
