-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: research_program (K404/K405/K406 follow-up), \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K415: 9 sector ETFs (XLB/XLE/XLF/XLI/XLK/XLP/XLU/XLV/XLY), 2010-2025, IS 2010-2019 (n=2495), OOS 2020-2025 (n=1485).\n\nCSVD = cross-sectional stdev of 22d sector realized vols. RelDisp = CSVD/mean_vol.\n\nKEY RESULTS:\n1. CSVD-VIX: r=0.730 (moderate). RelDisp-VIX: r=0.161 (nearly orthogonal).\n2. Daily |return| partial r(CSVD)|VIX: IS=-0.051(t=-2.55), OOS=-0.137(t=-5.31), Full=-0.104(t=-6.57 Harvey pass). NEGATIVE: higher CSVD = lower next-day |return|. Counter-intuitive.\n3. Monthly vol (non-overlapping): IS pr=-0.018(t=-0.19 NS), OOS pr=-0.384(t=-3.35 Harvey pass). IS completely insignificant despite OOS pass. dR2 OOS=0.087.\n4. Return prediction: raw r=0.17(p=0.02) but partial_r|VIX=-0.015(t=-0.19 NS). VIX absorbs entirely.\n5. Crash prob: Both IS and OOS: HIGH CSVD = MORE crashes (stress, not herding). Herding hypothesis REJECTED. Extreme DD events mean CSVD pctl=0.683 (high, not low).\n6. Strategy overlay: 6 variants ALL underperform base 50/50+VT OOS Sharpe. Best DM: S2 t=2.60 (fails Harvey t>3). VIX sufficient #29.\n7. Quintile: CSVD->return Spearman=0.130(p=0.08 NS), ANOVA p=0.41. CSVD->vol Spearman=0.434(p<0.001). VIX->vol Spearman=0.615 (stronger than CSVD).\n8. Window robustness: partial_r flips sign across windows (w=5:+0.028, w=22:-0.052, w=66:-0.153). Unstable.\n9. Rolling 3yr: 50% positive windows. Regime-dependent: positive 2013-2017, negative 2018-2023, positive again 2024.\n10. IS/OOS quintile: IS ret_spread=+0.012, OOS ret_spread=+0.032. Spearman->ret IS=0.096(NS), OOS=0.180(NS).\n\nHERDING HYPOTHESIS REJECTED: Low dispersion does NOT precede crashes. High dispersion (sector stress) precedes crashes. t=6.91 for bottom 25%.\nRELATIVE DISPERSION: Orthogonal to VIX (r=0.16) but zero predictive power. Orthogonality != utility.\nCONCLUSION: Null result. VIX sufficient #29. Extends K406 (dispersion OOS -22%) and K164 (monthly overlap artifact).",
