-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: User(I2 task), \u57f7\u884c: Claude] I2: Taiwan Futures Optimal Hedge Ratio (\u53f0\u6307\u671f\u6700\u9069\u907f\u96aa\u6bd4\u7387)\nTags: taiwan, hedge-ratio, futures, 0050, GARCH, VT, cross-hedge, OOS\nImportance: \u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\n\nData: yfinance (0050.TW, ^TWII, EWT, SPY, GLD, ^VIX) | 2010-2026 | N=3956 days\nCleaned: removed 2014-01-02 split artifact (-75% false return from yfinance Close)\nMethods: Naive(h=1), Rolling OLS(60d), EWMA(\u03bb=0.94), GJR-GARCH, VT-GARCH(8.63/VIX)\nOOS: IS 2010-2018, OOS1 2019-2021 (COVID), OOS2 2022-2025\n\n\u2605\u2605 After data cleaning: 0050.TW-TWII corr=0.9445 (was 0.653 before cleaning)\n\nHEDGE RATIO COMPARISON (TW50-TWII, full sample):\n| Method     | VarRed  | Sharpe_H | MDD_H   | Avg_h |\n|------------|---------|----------|---------|-------|\n| Naive(h=1) | 89.2%   | 0.864    | -10.4%  | 1.000 |\n| OLS-60d    | 89.3%   | 0.825    | -9.7%   | 1.025 |\n| EWMA-94    | 89.3%   | 0.801    | -9.5%   | 1.028 |\n| GJR-GARCH  | 80.3%   | 0.958    | -12.3%  | 0.744 |\n| VT-GARCH   | 56.0%   | 1.142    | -18.5%  | 0.354 |\n\nREGIME (GJR-GARCH):\nNormal VIX<20 (N=2750): h=0.75, VarRed=78.5%, Sharpe=1.63\nElevated VIX 20-30 (N=897): h=0.74, VarRed=83.5%, Sharpe=0.65\nCrisis VIX>30 (N=249): h=0.65, VarRed=79.7%, Sharpe=-1.52\n\nOOS (GJR-GARCH, TW50-TWII):\nIS: VarRed=76.3%, Sharpe=0.810\nOOS1 COVID: VarRed=82.3%, Sharpe=1.090 \u2605\nOOS2 2022-25: VarRed=83.4%, Sharpe=1.263 \u2605\u2605\n\nSTRATEGY RANKING (combined portfolio):\n#1: 50/50 0050+GLD \u2014 Sharpe 0.940, MDD -21.0% (K177 confirmed)\n#2: 50/50+GLD+GARCH \u2014 Sharpe 0.925, MDD -20.2%\n#3: GARCH Hedge Only \u2014 Sharpe 0.896, MDD -14.0% \u2605\u2605 (best MDD w/o GLD)\n#4: 0050 Only \u2014 Sharpe 0.762, MDD -33.0%\n#5: 50/50+VT+Naive \u2014 Sharpe 0.746, MDD -19.2%\n#6: 50/50+VT \u2014 Sharpe 0.707, MDD -21.0%\n#7: 50/50+VT+GARCH \u2014 Sharpe 0.684, MDD -19.1%\n\nDM TESTS:\nNaive vs GARCH (variance): DM=-9.57 \u2605\u2605\u2605 (Naive better for pure variance)\nOLS vs GARCH (variance): DM=-9.75 \u2605\u2605\u2605 (OLS better for pure variance)\nUtility (return-3*var): All NS \u2192 trade-off between variance reduction and return\nVT+Futures vs VT only: DM=+6.95 \u2605\u2605\u2605 (Futures adds significant variance reduction)\n50/50 vs 50/50+VT (variance): DM=+21.1 \u2605\u2605\u2605 (VT is massively effective)\n\nCROSS-HEDGE: EWT R\u00b2=12.3% (moderate), SPY R\u00b2=1.3% (useless). SPY NOT viable for Taiwan.\n\nGARCH h STABILITY: Mean=0.744, Std=0.122, IQR=[0.666, 0.808]\n\nCOST: Futures ~0.5-0.7%/yr vs VT cash drag ~1.9%/yr. Futures cheaper for variance reduction.\n\nCONCLUSIONS:\n1. GARCH h\u22480.74 is optimal for risk-adjusted return on TW50-TWII\n2. For pure variance minimization, naive h=1 sufficient (VarRed 89%)\n3. 50/50 0050+GLD (Sharpe 0.94) remains champion \u2014 adding VT or futures layers gives diminishing returns\n4. GARCH hedge only achieves best MDD (-14%) for equity-only investors\n5. Taiwan 0% capital gains tax is structural advantage for all strategies",
+    "content": "[提出: User(I2 task), 執行: Claude] I2: Taiwan Futures Optimal Hedge Ratio (台指期最適避險比率)\nTags: taiwan, hedge-ratio, futures, 0050, GARCH, VT, cross-hedge, OOS\nImportance: ★★★★\n\nData: yfinance (0050.TW, ^TWII, EWT, SPY, GLD, ^VIX) | 2010-2026 | N=3956 days\nCleaned: removed 2014-01-02 split artifact (-75% false return from yfinance Close)\nMethods: Naive(h=1), Rolling OLS(60d), EWMA(λ=0.94), GJR-GARCH, VT-GARCH(8.63/VIX)\nOOS: IS 2010-2018, OOS1 2019-2021 (COVID), OOS2 2022-2025\n\n★★ After data cleaning: 0050.TW-TWII corr=0.9445 (was 0.653 before cleaning)\n\nHEDGE RATIO COMPARISON (TW50-TWII, full sample):\n| Method     | VarRed  | Sharpe_H | MDD_H   | Avg_h |\n|------------|---------|----------|---------|-------|\n| Naive(h=1) | 89.2%   | 0.864    | -10.4%  | 1.000 |\n| OLS-60d    | 89.3%   | 0.825    | -9.7%   | 1.025 |\n| EWMA-94    | 89.3%   | 0.801    | -9.5%   | 1.028 |\n| GJR-GARCH  | 80.3%   | 0.958    | -12.3%  | 0.744 |\n| VT-GARCH   | 56.0%   | 1.142    | -18.5%  | 0.354 |\n\nREGIME (GJR-GARCH):\nNormal VIX<20 (N=2750): h=0.75, VarRed=78.5%, Sharpe=1.63\nElevated VIX 20-30 (N=897): h=0.74, VarRed=83.5%, Sharpe=0.65\nCrisis VIX>30 (N=249): h=0.65, VarRed=79.7%, Sharpe=-1.52\n\nOOS (GJR-GARCH, TW50-TWII):\nIS: VarRed=76.3%, Sharpe=0.810\nOOS1 COVID: VarRed=82.3%, Sharpe=1.090 ★\nOOS2 2022-25: VarRed=83.4%, Sharpe=1.263 ★★\n\nSTRATEGY RANKING (combined portfolio):\n#1: 50/50 0050+GLD — Sharpe 0.940, MDD -21.0% (K177 confirmed)\n#2: 50/50+GLD+GARCH — Sharpe 0.925, MDD -20.2%\n#3: GARCH Hedge Only — Sharpe 0.896, MDD -14.0% ★★ (best MDD w/o GLD)\n#4: 0050 Only — Sharpe 0.762, MDD -33.0%\n#5: 50/50+VT+Naive — Sharpe 0.746, MDD -19.2%\n#6: 50/50+VT — Sharpe 0.707, MDD -21.0%\n#7: 50/50+VT+GARCH — Sharpe 0.684, MDD -19.1%\n\nDM TESTS:\nNaive vs GARCH (variance): DM=-9.57 ★★★ (Naive better for pure variance)\nOLS vs GARCH (variance): DM=-9.75 ★★★ (OLS better for pure variance)\nUtility (return-3*var): All NS → trade-off between variance reduction and return\nVT+Futures vs VT only: DM=+6.95 ★★★ (Futures adds significant variance reduction)\n50/50 vs 50/50+VT (variance): DM=+21.1 ★★★ (VT is massively effective)\n\nCROSS-HEDGE: EWT R²=12.3% (moderate), SPY R²=1.3% (useless). SPY NOT viable for Taiwan.\n\nGARCH h STABILITY: Mean=0.744, Std=0.122, IQR=[0.666, 0.808]\n\nCOST: Futures ~0.5-0.7%/yr vs VT cash drag ~1.9%/yr. Futures cheaper for variance reduction.\n\nCONCLUSIONS:\n1. GARCH h≈0.74 is optimal for risk-adjusted return on TW50-TWII\n2. For pure variance minimization, naive h=1 sufficient (VarRed 89%)\n3. 50/50 0050+GLD (Sharpe 0.94) remains champion — adding VT or futures layers gives diminishing returns\n4. GARCH hedge only achieves best MDD (-14%) for equity-only investors\n5. Taiwan 0% capital gains tax is structural advantage for all strategies",
