-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: \u7528\u6236, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] READ-ONLY synthesis mapping 50 knowledge entries (K526-K583) to 3 papers. 35 findings relevant.\n\n**Paper 1 (Leverage Direction, 62p, JBF):** 6 strengthen, 7 add new sections, 4 require caveats. HIGHEST PRIORITY: (1) Add K530/K532/K533 HAR to Complexity Ceiling table \u2014 HAR dominates GARCH for prediction (DM=-15.45) but produces WORST VT strategy, the strongest evidence FOR the ceiling. (2) Add K548/K551 VIX-Conditional Leverage section (Harvey t=7.90, 11/11 OOS) with K567 international caveat (0/6 pass). (3) Add K573/K574 insurance pricing decomposition (breakeven VIX=26.6, 3-tier backtest table). 8 null results confirm VIX sufficiency (#34-#37+).\n\n**Paper 2 (Taiwan VT, 34p, PBFJ):** K553/K558 are potential 4th contribution \u2014 Taiwan Hybrid Leverage fully validated (t=4.79, 18/18 OOS, 0056 confirmed). US-style absolute VIX thresholds FAIL; rolling percentile needed. Methodological contribution for all emerging markets.\n\n**Paper 3 (VT \u2260 Trend, 24p):** K533 strengthens core argument (best predictor = worst strategy). K568 shows 12/VIX is return-OPTIMAL (not just parsimonious). K573 provides precise insurance cost (breakeven VIX=26.6). 3 null results confirm 12/VIX irreducibility.\n\n**4 cross-paper themes:** (1) Complexity Ceiling strengthened by HAR evidence, (2) Conditional leverage US+Taiwan validated with international boundary, (3) Insurance pricing quantified precisely, (4) VIX sufficiency count raised to ~37.",
