-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: User (K590 literature), \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K592: MF2-GARCH (Conrad & Engle JAE 2025) 2-step estimation \u2014 NULL RESULT. MF2-GARCH decomposes sigma^2_t = g_t * tau_t where g_t is short-run GJR on standardized returns z_t=r_t/sqrt(tau_t), tau_t=exp(omega+delta*log(RV22_{t-1})) is log-linear long-run component. 2-step: (1) OLS for tau, (2) MLE for GJR on z_t. SPY OOS 2023-2024 (502 days), w=2000, refit every 22 days. QLIKE: MF2=1.6697, GJR=1.5655, HAR-ABS=1.8348. MF2 WORSE than GJR by +6.65% (DM t=+2.53, p=0.011, fails Harvey t>3). MF2 beats HAR-ABS (DM t=-3.00). GJR persistence=0.75 in MF2 short-run (lower than standard ~0.97 because tau absorbs long-run). Sub-period: 2023 MF2 +3.5% vs GJR, 2024 MF2 +9.6% vs GJR \u2014 worsens over time. Key finding: 2-step estimation introduces efficiency loss \u2014 tau estimated by OLS on noisy log(r^2) is suboptimal. Confirms K144 (joint QML, also null for SPY) and QLIKE ceiling. Different from K591 post-hoc (which used simple multiplication). 6th independent null for MF2/MIDAS class models.",
