-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K737 Maximum Diversification Portfolio: tested 4 methods (EW, MinVar, MaxDiv, RiskParity) \u00d7 7 asset subsets (2-9 assets) vs 50/50 SPY/GLD baseline. COMMON_START 2023-01-04 to 2026-03-27. Key findings: (1) NO multi-asset strategy beats 50/50 SPY/GLD on Sharpe (baseline 1.862). Adding assets dilutes returns without improving risk-adjusted performance. (2) More assets \u2192 lower MDD but lower Sharpe: 9-asset EW MDD=-8.33% (vs -12.89%) but Sharpe=1.285. MinVar 9-asset MDD=-5.72% but Sharpe=1.007. (3) TLT hurts in 2023-2026: 3-asset with TLT Sharpe=1.49-1.51 vs without TLT 1.67-1.80. (4) 1/N beats optimization at same asset count (DeMiguel et al 2009 confirmed). (5) Max Diversification allocates heavily to low-vol bonds (IEF 68%) \u2014 DR=1.85 but low return. (6) Cross-OOS: only max_div 9-asset passes 3/5, but its COMMON Sharpe is only 0.87. (7) Sensitivity: longer lookback (504) helps max_div (1.37 vs 0.87) but still far below 50/50. CONCLUSION: asset selection cannot beat 50/50 SPY/GLD in 2023-2026 \u2014 the GLD bull run (+61% in 2025) makes any dilution harmful. The diversification-return tradeoff is unfavorable: you buy lower MDD but pay too much in Sharpe.",
