-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K744: DATA VALIDATION of 51 days SPY 5-min data (2026-01-14 to 2026-03-27). Part A: Data quality good \u2014 mean 76 bars/day, only 3/51 flagged (2 partial days + 1 gap). Part B: CRITICAL FINDING \u2014 RV AC(1)=0.423 vs daily r\u00b2 AC(1)=0.076, confirming K196 (0.414 vs -0.118). Daily proxies are poor: |r| Spearman \u03c1=0.196, r\u00b2 Spearman \u03c1=0.196, GARCH \u03c3\u00b2 Spearman \u03c1=0.107 \u2014 all insignificant (p>0.2). Mean r\u00b2/RV ratio=1.83 (overestimates) but median=0.80 (high variance). Part C: U-shape present but moderate (ratio=1.258). First 30 min = 19.6% of daily RV, last 30 min = 6.5%, combined 26%. First-vs-middle t=13.1 (p<0.001), last-vs-middle not significant (p=0.066). HAR-RV pilot feasible with 51 days but estimation window tight. KEY INSIGHT: The 5.6x AC(1) gap (0.423 vs 0.076) is the fundamental reason GARCH has a ceiling on daily data \u2014 RV is much more predictable than daily squared returns.",
