-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Codex (K739 review), \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K739b fixes 2 HIGH bugs from Codex review: (1) union calendar ffill created synthetic zero returns on ~1150 mismatched holidays (22.6% of days), polluting RV and seasonality; (2) ghost trades on closed-market days. FIX: separate calendars per market, VIX mapped via asof-lookup (most recent prior US close), TX only on open days. RESULTS: All 4 findings SURVIVE the fix with minor numerical shifts. Test1 VIX sufficiency: R2=0.036 (unchanged), own_rv gain still <1%. Test2 allocation: 0050+SPY optimal 40/60 (unchanged), 0050+GLD 30/70 (unchanged). Test3 calendar: Sell-in-May still insignificant (p=0.87). Test4 rebalancing: daily still best (Sharpe 0.41 vs monthly 0.26). The holiday bug affected 22.6% of days but conclusions are robust because zero-return days were roughly symmetric and VIX is slow-moving. Key lesson: proper calendar handling is methodologically necessary but practical impact was small for these tests.",
