-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Codex (7th suggestion), \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K760: ALTERNATIVE RISK PREMIA ROTATION. Data: yfinance SPY/GLD/VIX/VIX3M 2007-2026 (4840 days). Hypothesis: harvesting 4 vol risk premia (variance carry, skew/term structure, equity, safe haven) and rotating by VIX regime can beat 12/VIX. 4 signals: (1) Variance Carry = (VIX-RV22d)/VIX mean=0.241 (2) Term Structure = max(0, 1-VIX/VIX3M) mean=0.099 (3) Equity = 12/VIX mean=0.682 (4) Safe Haven = 1-equity. 3 regimes: Low VIX<15 (32%), Normal 15-25 (50%), High >25 (18%). 3 strategies tested: Equal-Weight (Sharpe 0.762), Regime-Rotated (0.712), Carry-Weighted (0.773) \u2014 ALL below 12/VIX (0.829) and 50/50 (0.788). DM tests: all NS (p>0.75). Cross-OOS: 0-1/5 periods beat 50/50. KEY INSIGHT: variance carry and term structure signals are tiny (mean 0.24 and 0.10) vs 12/VIX (0.68) \u2014 averaging them dilutes the equity signal, reducing SPY allocation from 68% to 34%. This is effectively a MORE CONSERVATIVE portfolio, not a smarter one. VRP analysis: VIX>RV 84% of days (mean premium 3.6%), SPY returns +14%/yr when VRP>0 vs -1.9%/yr when VRP<=0, but t=1.29 (NS). Sensitivity: \u00b120% threshold change only \u00b13.8% Sharpe change (stable but still loses). COMMON_START 2023-2026: multi-premia Sharpe 1.90-1.94 vs 12/VIX 1.73, but 50/50 still best at 2.01. Confirms K175 (rotation adds noise) and T13 (VIX term structure no incremental value for VT). The fundamental problem: mixing 4 weak-to-moderate signals doesn't create a strong signal \u2014 it creates signal dilution. 12/VIX's simplicity IS its strength.",
