-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: \u6587\u737b\u641c\u5c0b arXiv:2602.03903, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] Conformal VaR calibration: model-agnostic post-hoc wrapper that adjusts any VaR forecast using expanding-window quantile of past (loss - VaR) residuals. SPY Normal 1% VaR: uncalibrated violation ratio 2.06x (Kupiec FAIL, Basel RED) \u2192 uniform conformal 1.24x (Kupiec PASS, Basel GREEN, 77% improvement). Three methods tested: (1) uniform quantile: simplest, 77% improvement, (2) time-decay (lambda=0.01): 70% improvement, (3) regime-weighted (VIX kernel + time decay): 62% improvement but best sub-period adaptation (Volmageddon 2.39x\u21920.99x). Key asymmetry: conformal fixes under-coverage (Normal 2x\u21921.2x) but worsens already-conservative models (Student-t 0.85x\u21921.3x). Portfolio 50/50 SPY/GLD: Normal 2.06x\u21921.32x (RED\u2192GREEN). 5% VaR: Student-t time-decay achieves near-perfect 1.00x ratio. Limitations: needs 250-day history, cannot fix violation clustering (independence), expanding window has regime inertia. Codex review fixed regime VIX lookahead bug (using lagged VIX for historical weights). OOS: 2016-2026, N=2576. Data: yfinance SPY/GLD/VIX.",
