-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Codex, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K798 tests whether decision-focused learning (skip prediction, directly optimize action) can beat standard 12/VIX on SPY+GLD. Three approaches tested on OOS 2023-2025 (n=751).\n\n\u6838\u5fc3\u767c\u73fe:\n1. DF-OLS (Mean-Variance direct): OOS Sharpe=2.196 vs 12/VIX 1.509 (+0.687), but DM t=-0.687 (p=0.49) \u2014 NOT significant. Mean weight=0.545 (near static 50/50).\n2. FC-Policy (OLS features\u2192optimal_w): OOS Sharpe=2.262, MDD=-7.9% (best MDD). DM t=-0.924 (p=0.36) \u2014 NOT significant. Mean weight=0.641 (overweight SPY in bull market).\n3. Contextual Bandit (\u03b5=0.1, 6 arms, 5 VIX contexts): OOS Sharpe=2.008. DM t=-0.171 (p=0.86) \u2014 NOT significant.\n4. BH 50/50 wins CRRA utility (gamma=5): -0.249100 vs all adaptive strategies.\n5. Harvey t>3.0 breaches: 0/5 DM tests. None significant.\n\n\u95dc\u9375\u6d1e\u898b:\n- All decision-focused methods appear better on Sharpe in 2023-2025 OOS, but this reflects a bull SPY market (S&P up ~70% in 2023-25) \u2014 methods that overweight SPY win trivially.\n- DF-OLS converges to mean_w=0.545 (nearly static), essentially a slight SPY tilt.\n- FC-Policy mean_w=0.641 is significantly overweighted in SPY \u2014 would lose in bear market.\n- Bandit learned contradictory policy: Q1 (low VIX) \u2192 arm=0.8, Q3 (medium VIX) \u2192 arm=0.2 (reduces SPY in medium VIX). Inconsistent.\n- No method passes Harvey t>3.0. 12/VIX irreducible result #7 (following K440/K470/K488/K524).\n- Conclusion: Decision-focused approaches do NOT provide statistically significant improvement over 12/VIX. Sample period (strong bull) creates misleading Sharpe numbers.\n\n\u6578\u64da\u4f86\u6e90: yfinance SPY/GLD/VIX 2007-2025, OOS 2023-01-03 to 2025-12-30 (n=751)\nCodex \u5be9\u67e5: \u901a\u904e (3 bugs fixed: DM test variance, TX cost inconsistency, FC feature timing)",
