-    "title": "K802: GJR + Skewed-t VaR \u2014 Dual Champion Achieved",
-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: \u7528\u6236, \u57f7\u884c: Claude]\n\nK802 resolves the K799 conflict: GJR wins QLIKE but fails VaR 1% under Normal distribution assumption. By replacing the Normal quantile with a fat-tail distribution, GJR achieves BOTH best QLIKE and VaR Trinity PASS simultaneously.\n\nKEY RESULTS (SPY 2023-2024, n=502 OOS days):\n- QLIKE: GJR=1.4686 vs GARCH=1.5137 (GJR wins, DM t=-3.25, p=0.001, Harvey t>3.0 PASS)\n- Spearman: GJR rho=0.2116 >> GARCH rho=0.1087\n\nVaR BACKTEST (1% level, Trinity = Kupiec + Christoffersen + Basel Green):\n- GJR+Normal: violations=9/502 (1.79%), Kupiec p=0.108 \u2192 Basel YELLOW \u2192 FAIL (replicates K799)\n- GJR+StudentT: violations=6/502 (1.20%), all PASS \u2192 Trinity PASS\n- GJR+SkewedT: violations=6/502 (1.20%), all PASS \u2192 Trinity PASS \u2190 DUAL CHAMPION\n- GARCH+Normal: violations=7/502 (1.39%), all PASS \u2192 Trinity PASS (K799 baseline)\n- GJR+FHS: violations=5/502 (1.00%), Kupiec p=0.993 \u2192 Trinity PASS\n\nDISTRIBUTION PARAMETERS (estimated from IS standardized residuals):\n- Student-t df \u2248 15\u201316 (fat tails, not ~5 as often assumed)\n- Skewed-t xi \u2248 0.99 (nearly symmetric \u2014 equity returns in 2023-2024 not strongly skewed)\n- FHS 1% quantile \u2248 -2.73 to -2.81 (vs Normal -2.33, confirming fat tails)\n\nCONCLUSION: GJR+Skewed-t is the Dual Champion \u2014 best \u03c3\u00b2 forecasting (QLIKE) AND correct VaR tail coverage. The Normal distribution underestimates tails (z=-2.33 too small), while Student-t df~16 and Skewed-t both give z~-2.58 to -2.60, achieving correct 1% VaR coverage. The high df (15-16) means tails are fatter than Normal but not as extreme as often parameterized (df=5). Xi~0.99 (near-symmetric) in the 2023-2024 period.\n",
+    "title": "K802: GJR + Skewed-t VaR — Dual Champion Achieved",
+    "content": "[提出: 用戶, 執行: Claude]\n\nK802 resolves the K799 conflict: GJR wins QLIKE but fails VaR 1% under Normal distribution assumption. By replacing the Normal quantile with a fat-tail distribution, GJR achieves BOTH best QLIKE and VaR Trinity PASS simultaneously.\n\nKEY RESULTS (SPY 2023-2024, n=502 OOS days):\n- QLIKE: GJR=1.4686 vs GARCH=1.5137 (GJR wins, DM t=-3.25, p=0.001, Harvey t>3.0 PASS)\n- Spearman: GJR rho=0.2116 >> GARCH rho=0.1087\n\nVaR BACKTEST (1% level, Trinity = Kupiec + Christoffersen + Basel Green):\n- GJR+Normal: violations=9/502 (1.79%), Kupiec p=0.108 → Basel YELLOW → FAIL (replicates K799)\n- GJR+StudentT: violations=6/502 (1.20%), all PASS → Trinity PASS\n- GJR+SkewedT: violations=6/502 (1.20%), all PASS → Trinity PASS ← DUAL CHAMPION\n- GARCH+Normal: violations=7/502 (1.39%), all PASS → Trinity PASS (K799 baseline)\n- GJR+FHS: violations=5/502 (1.00%), Kupiec p=0.993 → Trinity PASS\n\nDISTRIBUTION PARAMETERS (estimated from IS standardized residuals):\n- Student-t df ≈ 15–16 (fat tails, not ~5 as often assumed)\n- Skewed-t xi ≈ 0.99 (nearly symmetric — equity returns in 2023-2024 not strongly skewed)\n- FHS 1% quantile ≈ -2.73 to -2.81 (vs Normal -2.33, confirming fat tails)\n\nCONCLUSION: GJR+Skewed-t is the Dual Champion — best σ² forecasting (QLIKE) AND correct VaR tail coverage. The Normal distribution underestimates tails (z=-2.33 too small), while Student-t df~16 and Skewed-t both give z~-2.58 to -2.60, achieving correct 1% VaR coverage. The high df (15-16) means tails are fatter than Normal but not as extreme as often parameterized (df=5). Xi~0.99 (near-symmetric) in the 2023-2024 period.\n",
