-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K1071 decomposes K1070's right-tail effect. N=999 events, mean CASV=2.78 reproduced exactly. FIVE MAJOR FINDINGS: (1) Top 2 events (2014-10-30/31) contribute 64% of mean due to tiny estimation-window \u03c3 artifact (structural break preceding). (2) CRISIS REGIME CLUSTERING STRONGLY CONFIRMED: High-VIX (\u226525) events = 14.6% of pool, mean CASV=+8.40 (t=4.59, p<0.001); Low-VIX events mean CASV=+1.82 NS. All statistical significance lives in high-VIX subset. Fisher test Top-10% over-representation in high-VIX: p=6.8e-6. (3) Sector nuanced: Financials UNDER-represented in right tail (odds 0.60, p=1e-4); Traditional slightly over-represented (odds 1.44, p=0.002); Tech NS. (4) Systematic shocks drive top events: VIX level MW p=1.9e-10, SPY |return| MW p=2e-3; BUT announcement count NOT the mechanism (KS p=0.86) \u2014 clustering theory rejected. (5) AFTER STRIPPING TOP 10%: mean CASV = -2.28 (t=-15.37, p<0.001); 90% of earnings events have ETF vol BELOW normal. Trimmed 90% mean = -0.88 [CI: -1.41, -0.25]. PAPER 2 CORE IMPLICATION: Taiwan VT strategy (which de-levers in high VIX) ALREADY captures all earnings vol risk. No need for separate earnings-calendar overlay. Low-VIX earnings days are below-normal vol. Sector-targeted hedging hypothesis killed (Financials under-represented). This simplifies Paper 2's practical recommendation dramatically.",
