-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K1072 compares standard RV, Realized Kernel (BNHLS 2008 Parzen), and subsampled RV (Zhang et al. 2005) for SPY 58 days of 5-min data. KEY FINDINGS: (H1/H2) 5-min SPY microstructure noise NOT significant. Paired t_RV_RK = -0.16, p=0.87. Wilcoxon p=0.39. rel_gap (RV-RK)/RV mean=2.99%, median=8.43%, 63.8% days RV>RK (modest). \u03b3_1/\u03b3_0 mean=+0.0006, only 43.1% negative (bid-ask bounce would dominate negative). Consistent with Liu-Patton-Sheppard (2015): 5-min optimal for liquid indices. (H3) HAR-RK vs HAR-RV on RK target DM t=+1.999 p=0.056, below Harvey 3.0. (H4 CORE) K1054 A4f ranking PROXY-ROBUST: HAR-RV > GJR-GARCH > A4f-VIX\u00b2 on all 3 RV-family proxies (DM t on RK=-2.86, RV=-3.50, RV_sub=-3.31). Only r\u00b2 flips (target mismatch, mechanical). Paper 9 implication: K1054's A4f conclusion stable across proxy choice. 5-min RV = RK \u2248 RV_sub for practical purposes in SPY. PAPER 9 ROBUSTNESS APPENDIX candidate but not required (RV sufficient for main text). Limitations: 58 days/28 OOS << Harvey-safe; \u03c9\u00b2 noise estimate crude (floors to 0 on 57% days); TSRV not tested.",
