-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K1074 tests whether A4f's statistical QLIKE edge (K988 DM t=4.48) translates to VT strategy Sharpe. OOS 2013-2026 (n=3338 days). FIVE STRATEGIES tested with proper signal.shift(1) lag and 5bp TX cost. NET SHARPE: 12/VIX-VT 0.861 \u2605 (wins SPY-VT cohort) > A4f-VT 0.843 > GJR-VT 0.821. MDD: 12/VIX -16.30% < A4f -18.58% < GJR -18.15%. TURNOVER: A4f 16.3/yr vs 12/VIX 9.7/yr (+68%). H1-H4 CONFIRMED: A4f higher turnover, 5bp TX exactly cancels QLIKE edge. Net Sharpe diff -0.022, p=0.64, CI spans zero. H5 MARGINAL: 50/50+A4f 0.852 vs 50/50+12/VIX 0.814, diff 0.033 p=0.37 NS. BH 50/50 = 0.873 (overall best) \u2014 NOBODY beats BH 50/50 (K702 8th confirmation). All lookahead_guard PASS, sharpe_sanity PASS. Hit rate A4f vs 12/VIX monthly = 56.2% (coin flip). PAPER 3 IMPLICATION: K988's QLIKE edge does NOT translate to VT Sharpe edge. This STRENGTHENS Paper 3 thesis: VT alpha is TSMOM / return-side insurance, NOT sigma-forecast quality. More accurate sigma is not the bottleneck. KEY METHODOLOGY PRINCIPLE: Statistical significance \u2260 economic significance \u2014 always test both. PAPER 9 IMPLICATION: A4f's contribution is QLIKE (risk assessment accuracy) and VaR (K1058 Trinity PASS, K1055 interval width), NOT strategy Sharpe.",
