-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K1095 tests synthesis strategy: 8.63/VIX normally + A4f-VT only in [-5,+5] window around top-10 stock earnings. OOS 2017-2026 (N=2,160), net 20bp TX. ALL 3 HYPOTHESES REJECTED. SHARPE: Pure 8.63/VIX 0.929, Pure A4f-VT 0.966, Event-Switched 0.777 (WORST), BH 1.020. H1 (Switched > 8.63/VIX) FAIL. H2 (Switched > A4f-VT) DM t=-2.89 p=0.004 switched STATISTICALLY WORSE. H3 (Events concentrate A4f alpha) REJECTED \u2014 every strategy has LOWER Sharpe on event days (0.46-0.65) vs non-event (1.32-1.49). WHY FAIL: (1) Event coverage 49-71% too high \u2014 top-10 stocks announce too frequently so [-5,+5] windows not sparse. (2) Event days are VOLATILITY regimes not RETURN regimes \u2014 low Sharpe everywhere. (3) Turnover doubles 13.4x vs 6.5x \u2192 20bp TX removes ~130bp/yr. CRITICAL INSIGHT: K1062 Part D's A4f QLIKE advantage is GLOBAL not event-specific. DM t=+2.71 on A4f-VT vs 8.63/VIX spread holds regardless of event timing. K1068's CAR\u22480 CASV>>0 pattern means event days show 'vol spike but no return drift' \u2014 which doesn't help VT strategy. IMPLICATION: Do NOT add event-overlay to Taiwan VT. Keep 8.63/VIX or A4f-VT pure. A4f-VT wins overall Sharpe (0.966>0.929) but 2x higher MDD (-27.9% vs -16.5%). Simple rule still best for risk-conscious investors.",
