-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K1097 pivoted from duplicating K1019 to extending with Student-t innovations + full Trinity. Agent detected K1019 already did MS-GJR vs GJR + A4f-VIX (per CLAUDE.md \u4e0d\u91cd\u8907\u539f\u5247). RESULTS: M3 MS-GJR-t QLIKE=1.630 vs M2 MS-GJR-N=1.614 \u2192 Student-t does NOT improve MS-GJR (DM t=+0.62 NS). M4 A4f-VIX9D-t remains best: QLIKE=1.568, full Trinity PASS at 1% and 5%, lowest FZ0 (-5.07). NEITHER MS variant fixes VaR: M3 Kupiec 1% p=0.04, 5% p=0.02. NOVEL EMPIRICAL FINDING: MS-GJR-t has regime-label instability across refits \u2014 mean P(calm) jumps 0.835\u21920.149 within 6 months. Student-t absorbing fat tails causes the 2 regimes to differentiate by persistence (one near-unit-root, one mean-reverting) rather than volatility level, breaking unconditional-variance-based ordering. PAPER 9 IMPLICATION: Strengthens case for A4f-VIX9D-t as single recommended equity model. Beats MS-GJR family even with matching Student-t. Only model passing full VaR-ES Trinity.",
