-    "content": "[\u63d0\u51fa: Claude, \u57f7\u884c: Claude] K1098 tests Paper 10 hypothesis: can TAIFEX VIXTWN rescue K1077 NULL on 0050.TW? Used 15 years of official Dropbox data (2007-2021), OOS 2013-2021 (~8 yrs). ALL 4 HYPOTHESES FAIL. A4f-VIXTWN DM t=+1.86 below Harvey. Head-to-head vs A4f-VIX: t=-0.99 (VIX slightly BETTER). COMBO +0.14/+1.51 no improvement. Spearman ranks with r\u00b2: VIX 0.211 > VIXTWN 0.201. REGIME TEST: even when VIXTWN-VIX spread top 20% (n=441), VIXTWN still loses DM t=-1.30. COMPLETE CROSS-ASSET MATRIX: GLD+GVZ +4.46 PASS, USO+OVX +4.48 PASS, **0050.TW+VIXTWN +1.86 FAIL**. PAPER 9 CONFIRMATION: Taiwan gap is STRUCTURAL \u2014 K1083 showed currency (USD/TWD) explains 83%, TSMC concentration is residual 17%. A domestic equity IV can't fix a currency-denomination problem. VIXTWN level-correlation with VIX=0.87 so VIXTWN adds marginal info even locally. PAPER 10 SIDE PAPER: NOT SUPPORTED by evidence. Taiwan is boundary case in Paper 9 matrix, not independent paper material. METHODOLOGY NOTE: Codex pre-review caught 2 bugs (Harvey sign for wrong-direction + VIXTWN Oct/Nov 2007 format). Fixed before run. DOWNSTREAM: K1099 USD/TWD realized vol directly; K1100 TWSE-50 ex-TSMC; K1101 single-stock TSMC with VIXTWN (isolate concentration).",
